I. SEITEH NAME ETYMOLOGY
= ehr. ct'eh - whole world          | ct' + eh
= ghl. sh'sta'h - origin of all     | sh' + sta'h

Ct' >> (sst)
Eh  >> (eh)

= ehr. "ssteh"
= ghl. "shhstaah"
= ghl. "sejitaah" (IV era) <seyta'h>
= bae. "seiteh" (ehr./ghl.)

II. TARSKIGG & NORDWINIAN LANGUAGE
Tarskigg = tar + skigg

> Tar - elders
> Skigg - meeting, gathering

Plural is default of some words, such as 'tar', resembling
tribalic mindset

-od is suffix used to signify "I do something"

For example:
             Kalahod (kalahod)

"I do the ritual"

Kalah - to do ritual (kala:, "...h" is silent)
-od   - signify first-person actor

Kalahagad - wrath of gods, usually due to sacrilege (kalahaga:d)
Agad - wrath (aga:d)
Lig - strong (Heim-lig baedoorian name suffix)

